1
00:00:01,630 --> 00:00:04,550
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:46,770 --> 00:01:47,690
[grunts]

3
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,070
That was a daemon.

4
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:56,070
Yes, I think so. Good eye.

5
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,950
Pull over.
I'd like a closer look.

6
00:01:59,040 --> 00:01:59,910
Right.

7
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,130
It's a beautiful evening, ma'am.

8
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,420
And that's a fine companion
you've got there.

9
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:13,630
[Yozakura growls]

10
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:14,630
[WOMAN] Uh?

11
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,140
You can see them?

12
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:21,140
Feathers as black
as the night sky

13
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,890
and a fearsome horned skull.

14
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,520
A handsome daemon,
if I may be so bold.

15
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,520
What's their name?

16
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:27,860
[woman gasps]

17
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,980
[Yozakura growls]

18
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:31,570
[woman crying]

19
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:37,620
Finally...
You're the first person I've met

20
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:39,410
who doesn't think I'm crazy.

21
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,540
♪

22
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,040
[GONZO]
Of course I don't.

23
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,920
I'm just like you.

24
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,000
[chuckles softly]

25
00:02:50,090 --> 00:02:51,300
[WOMAN] Uh?

26
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:52,920
[gasps]

27
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,670
[YOZAKURA] Hm. Hm.

28
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,930
[woman sighs]

29
00:03:00,010 --> 00:03:01,010
♪

30
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:04,270
[YOZAKURA] We are Kin'u-gyokuto.

31
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:07,020
[WOMAN] This one is named
Yozakura.

32
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,690
[GONZO] Hmm.
I don't see their other half.

33
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:13,030
[WOMAN] Asagiri.
They don't like the night,

34
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:14,400
so they're hiding.

35
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:18,870
[sighs] I see.
And what are you doing out here

36
00:03:18,950 --> 00:03:21,450
on the bridge at this hour?
It's dangerous.

37
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:26,290
[WOMAN] I was thinking
about jumping.

38
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:27,500
Ending it all.

39
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,920
It's not as though
anybody needs me around.

40
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,130
[YOZAKURA] If you were to fall,
I would catch you in an instant.

41
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,260
You must live.

42
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,720
[WOMAN] Forgive me.
I'm so sorry. [cries]

43
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:45,100
I shouldn't be saying
such things to you. We just met.

44
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:46,980
[GONZO]
Please, you're fine.

45
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,770
It must be fate that I happened
to pass by here.

46
00:03:49,850 --> 00:03:51,060
I'm happy to sit and talk

47
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:52,690
if you'd like
to share some more.

48
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:53,860
♪

49
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:56,400
I'm Gonzo Kagemori, by the way.

50
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:59,610
[WOMAN] Oh, I'm Iori Shingo.

51
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,530
You're really convinced
nobody needs you?

52
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:04,540
Uh, it's true.

53
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,790
I've never been able
to do anything right,

54
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,290
even as a child.

55
00:04:08,370 --> 00:04:11,460
I failed my parents every way
I possibly could.

56
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:13,790
Like, not getting
into a good school.

57
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:16,510
No surprise, since I'm stupid.

58
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,800
Even my older brother says so.

59
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,430
They all treat me like I never
should have been born

60
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:22,550
in the first place.

61
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,850
So, yeah.

62
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:28,850
I think the world would be
a better place if I was gone.

63
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:30,060
♪

64
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:32,860
I've thought about this a lot.

65
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:36,400
In fact, I tried to die once
and couldn't even do that right.

66
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:37,940
♪

67
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,870
I met my companions
when I went into the mountains

68
00:04:42,950 --> 00:04:45,120
looking for a place
to end my life.

69
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:48,080
There,
I stumbled across their relic.

70
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,750
It didn't have hands or a head,

71
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:56,420
but something about it
was breathtaking.

72
00:04:57,510 --> 00:04:59,720
I don't know much
about gods or Buddhas,

73
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,970
but I guess I kind of thought...

74
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,350
if I were to die in front
of such a statue,

75
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:07,770
maybe it would escort my soul
to heaven.

76
00:05:07,850 --> 00:05:08,890
♪

77
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:12,230
So I slit my wrist, but then...

78
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:14,860
Your two daemons appeared.

79
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:16,190
That's right.

80
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:19,110
They're very kind
and excellent listeners.

81
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:21,900
I told them
about my struggles in life.

82
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:23,280
Later,

83
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:25,530
my family overheard me
talking to them,

84
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,160
which didn't go well.

85
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,290
They were sure I'd lost my mind.

86
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,410
♪

87
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,420
I tried to explain
what daemons are,

88
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,170
but that was hopeless
since they couldn't see them.

89
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:36,920
They thought
I was hallucinating,

90
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,340
hearing things, sick.

91
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,720
So I revealed them to my family,
thinking that would help.

92
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,890
Instead, they called them
devils and evil spirits.

93
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:48,220
They said I'd been possessed
by monsters.

94
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:51,430
And before long,
I was even more ostracized.

95
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,770
Only my brother
seemed interested,

96
00:05:53,850 --> 00:05:55,190
though I'm still not sure why.

97
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:57,650
[YOZAKURA] He cannot be trusted!

98
00:05:57,730 --> 00:06:01,110
He pretends to understand
only because he wishes

99
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:03,650
to work us to death
for his own benefit.

100
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:06,030
He would take
advantage of you, Iori.

101
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:09,080
You must cut ties
with the Shingos!

102
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,250
What life is there
without my family?

103
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:14,170
This world has no use
for people like me.

104
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:15,500
[exhales]

105
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,170
♪

106
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:20,630
This is sudden, but I would like
to invite you into my home.

107
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,420
Uh, huh?

108
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:25,880
The Kagemoris are a pretty
big clan, growing every day.

109
00:06:25,970 --> 00:06:27,390
We're always on the lookout

110
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:29,600
for new members
and people to join us.

111
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:33,350
All right. That said,
I'm a total stranger to you.

112
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,480
We have plenty
of other employees

113
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,480
who come from backgrounds
and situations similar to yours.

114
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,650
Many of them are Wielders
like yourself.

115
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:43,320
You'll find we're
an incredibly welcoming group.

116
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:44,990
[chuckles]

117
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,490
That's especially true
when someone has daemons.

118
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:59,210
[ASA] Brother, your shoulder...
Are you okay?

119
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:03,050
Yeah, I think I'll be fine.
I can still move my arm.

120
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,920
Wait, were you shot
with a rifle?

121
00:07:05,010 --> 00:07:06,680
You need proper treatment.

122
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,890
But if we go
to a regular doctor,

123
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,390
they'd ask probing questions
and get the police involved,

124
00:07:11,470 --> 00:07:13,310
which would cause
all kinds of problems.

125
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:14,390
[Yuru gasps]

126
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,060
Plus, you don't have
any insurance,

127
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,020
so treatment would be
super expensive.

128
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,230
Wait, I don't want that.

129
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:21,900
Hana would never forgive me.

130
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:25,150
[ASA] There's only
one thing left.

131
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,150
You're coming back to the manor!

132
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,240
[YURU] Why would I?

133
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,240
Because Dr. Sakurazawa
can treat you in the infirmary.

134
00:07:31,330 --> 00:07:33,660
Plus, she's used to dealing
with stuff like this.

135
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:36,580
Huh? The woman
who steals your blood?

136
00:07:36,670 --> 00:07:39,460
Hold on, are you even positive
that she's a real doctor?

137
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,500
'Cause I am not.

138
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,050
And besides...

139
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,840
It's not like I can trust
the Kagemoris

140
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,130
-in the first place.
-[grunting]

141
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,510
[YURU] Thanks, but I'm gonna
have to pass.

142
00:07:48,590 --> 00:07:51,050
[ASA] You're being
so mean, brother.

143
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:53,850
You have so much faith in them.
You sure that's wise?

144
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,850
Yes, of course I am.

145
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:01,150
I get it.
They're a little strange.

146
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:03,020
And they aren't like others
down here.

147
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:05,190
But that's for the best.

148
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:07,860
Normal people don't last long
in this world.

149
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,660
Like I told you before,

150
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,030
it was the master
and Jin who saved me

151
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,120
from Higashi Village assassins.

152
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,870
[YURU] Jin? Hm...

153
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:19,920
He didn't deny
that he was responsible

154
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,580
for the attack on the village.

155
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,340
Even when I was holding
a machete to his neck.

156
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,880
[ASA] Exactly. He's earnest
in the strangest ways.

157
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,470
When it comes
to the three brothers,

158
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:32,720
he's the one who plays the role
of the bad guy

159
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:36,560
to protect the Kagemoris.
Every time. Without fail.

160
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,430
He stays detached

161
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,440
and avoids empathizing
with foes and subordinates.

162
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:43,270
It's like he suppresses
his emotions

163
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:46,230
for the sake of the clan.
He does what he must.

164
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,190
And what about the other two?

165
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,450
[ASA] Hagure teaches me
new skills

166
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,950
so that one day I'll be able
to live a normal life.

167
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:54,120
It's been really helpful.

168
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,450
He showed me how to draw manga.

169
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,370
Those are, uh, picture books.

170
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:01,040
You could say they're like
modern woodblock prints.

171
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,670
He lets me help him
with his work.

172
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,250
That way, I can earn money

173
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,960
inside the barrier
where it's safe.

174
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:08,090
[YURU] Wow, that's nice.

175
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:09,630
And Asuma...

176
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:12,050
His smile looks fake.

177
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:14,640
He's the least trustworthy
one of the whole bunch.

178
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,390
[ASA] Did he stand there with
that serene look on his face

179
00:09:17,470 --> 00:09:18,980
and ask if you wanted to die?

180
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,600
[YURU] Oh. Oh, yeah, he did!

181
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,440
Asuma thinks if people are going
to keep trying to kill you,

182
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,940
you should just let it happen.

183
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:26,770
That way, you can acquire
more power

184
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,860
so you're able
to protect yourself better.

185
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:32,280
He also argues that people
like us should be subject

186
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,620
to the oversight
of a powerful organization,

187
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,780
one like the Kagemoris,
for example.

188
00:09:36,870 --> 00:09:38,540
He may say unsettling things,

189
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:42,410
but he doesn't lie to us.
I really do believe that.

190
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:46,210
[ASUMA] What shall we do
with the girl?

191
00:09:46,290 --> 00:09:47,960
Return her to Higashi?

192
00:09:48,710 --> 00:09:49,880
[Dera sighs]

193
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,880
I'm afraid she's seen and heard
too much down here.

194
00:09:52,970 --> 00:09:54,970
If we took her back
to the village,

195
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:56,600
we'd have to make sure
she doesn't say--

196
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,720
[GONZO]
You'd throw her in a cell?

197
00:09:58,810 --> 00:10:00,100
♪

198
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:04,650
Is there a way
she can keep her freedom?

199
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:06,270
The children of Higashi village

200
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:08,070
don't know the twins'
secret yet.

201
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:10,070
They have no idea
that Asa and Yuru

202
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,650
gain immense power
by dying.

203
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,530
People are only
let in on the truth

204
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:14,910
once they've gotten older.

205
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:17,410
It's how the villagers
recognize you as an adult.

206
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:20,200
I seriously doubt Azami
understands anything.

207
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,540
[FUYUKI]
So they do share the secret.

208
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,790
[GONZO] Learning it means
you've entered adulthood

209
00:10:24,870 --> 00:10:26,920
and are an official member
of the village.

210
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,340
They're creating unity
by making people think

211
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,420
they've been given
special knowledge.

212
00:10:31,510 --> 00:10:32,760
[Gonzo grunts]

213
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,470
That could be hard to accept.

214
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,390
And what if somebody questions
the village's ways?

215
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:40,100
Anyone who dissents
is kicked down the mountain

216
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:42,930
under the guise that they're
being sent here to work.

217
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:45,350
They survive by doing
whatever odd jobs

218
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:48,060
associates of the village
are able to scrounge up.

219
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:49,690
Huh? Hold on a minute.

220
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,400
A lot of people left the village
for work.

221
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:54,320
Are you saying
they never came back 'cause--

222
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:56,030
[DERA] If they were
allowed to return,

223
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:57,910
they might reveal the truth
to Yuru.

224
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:00,780
Don't get me wrong,
there are some guys

225
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:03,750
who come down here looking
for legitimate employment.

226
00:11:04,370 --> 00:11:05,660
[sighs]

227
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:09,630
The Kagemoris usually
kill them, though.

228
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,000
Make no mistake.

229
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:13,670
We both have plenty of blood
on our hands.

230
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:17,380
The Taderas have murdered
many of our people as well.

231
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:20,600
[Dera chuckles]

232
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:23,020
[Gonzo chuckles]

233
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:25,390
[both laugh]

234
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,520
[RIGHT] Uh?

235
00:11:32,570 --> 00:11:34,990
Hey, you two have
a nice chat in there?

236
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:38,070
-Sure did.
-You did a great job. Thank you.

237
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:40,910
[Daifuku
and Ohagi squeal]

238
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:44,290
[ASA] Oh, Master! My brother
has a pretty bad wound.

239
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,160
I'd like him to be treated
back home.

240
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:48,120
I never agreed to go with you!

241
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:50,080
Sorry, but we can't.

242
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:52,500
I'll have to deal
with Akio first thing.

243
00:11:52,590 --> 00:11:55,380
I'd prefer if Yuru
didn't have to see that.

244
00:11:55,470 --> 00:11:58,220
Oh. I had almost forgotten.

245
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,930
[YURU] Akio? The bald guy
who wanted me dead?

246
00:12:02,010 --> 00:12:03,470
[GONZO]
We tracked down the traitor

247
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,770
at the manor earlier.

248
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,810
It was Akio after all.

249
00:12:06,890 --> 00:12:09,770
Ah. So Jin's suspicion
was correct.

250
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:12,150
Though, it's strange.

251
00:12:12,230 --> 00:12:13,980
I'd think my uncle
would've told me

252
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:17,110
if he were in league with Akio,
yet his name never came up.

253
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,320
That night Yuru visited us,

254
00:12:20,410 --> 00:12:22,370
it was my uncle
who tipped me off

255
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,910
that both twins
would be in the same place.

256
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:28,410
He said Ivan was the one
who told him,

257
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:31,500
and that they were sending
some mercs he scraped together.

258
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:34,210
He suggested that's when
I should betray you.

259
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:37,590
Well, I of course
ignored his message

260
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:39,170
and pretended to be asleep.

261
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,510
You left him on unread?

262
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:45,890
If not Shingo, then Akio
must know Ivan personally.

263
00:12:45,970 --> 00:12:48,100
-[gasps] Ivan!
-I got it.

264
00:12:48,730 --> 00:12:51,690
Akio's working with the guy
who knows about our parents.

265
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,320
Which means he might know
something, too.

266
00:12:56,270 --> 00:12:57,280
[FUYUKI] Master...

267
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,530
We should return at once.

268
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:04,990
If they have any info,
I will get it out of them.

269
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,630
[clattering]

270
00:13:16,590 --> 00:13:18,880
[Hagure gasps]

271
00:13:18,970 --> 00:13:21,130
[screams]

272
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,470
My studio!

273
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:26,970
My work!
That computer had my drafts!

274
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,850
[GABBY] Yeah, a fight broke out.

275
00:13:28,930 --> 00:13:30,980
That's a big whoops from us.

276
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:35,650
But not everything's gone.
The coffee maker's still okay.

277
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,990
You want me to make you a cup?

278
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:40,610
A curse upon you
and all your family,

279
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:42,280
that every last cup of coffee
you drink

280
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,240
turns into ink
for the rest of your life!

281
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:46,450
Where are the files? [groans]

282
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:47,620
They're safe. Good.

283
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,540
[GABBY] Even if they were gone,

284
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,040
couldn't you have
just redrawn them

285
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,410
with Black and White?

286
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,710
Mm... You don't get it.

287
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:58,250
Imperfections of a manga drawn
by hand are what make it good.

288
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,920
I'm not so sure about that.
I like it sharp.

289
00:14:01,010 --> 00:14:03,340
When everything
clicks into place.

290
00:14:03,430 --> 00:14:05,340
But that doesn't feel
true to life.

291
00:14:05,430 --> 00:14:06,930
When I create my characters,

292
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:09,220
it's what I try
to pay attention to the most.

293
00:14:09,310 --> 00:14:10,480
[running footsteps]

294
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:13,480
It's more real when their hearts
wobble and waver.

295
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:17,070
Jin! Please, listen to me!

296
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,440
There's gotta be something
you can do to save Akio!

297
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:20,990
There isn't a chance.

298
00:14:21,070 --> 00:14:23,610
The old man would never forgive
someone who betrayed us.

299
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,620
Akio will die for what he did.

300
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,990
We've been together
ever since we were kids.

301
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,790
We may not be related by blood,
but he's my brother!

302
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:33,410
I know there's no way
the master would listen to me.

303
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,290
But if it came from his son,
then he would--

304
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:36,460
[JIN] Haruo.

305
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:39,340
We can't keep
threats around the manor.

306
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,960
It puts yours and everyone
else's lives at risk.

307
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:46,300
Akio can't be allowed to live.

308
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,720
[Haruo gasps]

309
00:14:49,850 --> 00:14:50,760
[clattering]

310
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:53,730
[SAKURAZAWA] There's not much
I can do about a severed arm.

311
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,980
I stopped the bleeding.

312
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:58,690
You want more than that,
take him to the hospital.

313
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,030
To think my own kid brother
was the one

314
00:15:05,110 --> 00:15:07,570
who betrayed our clan. [sighs]

315
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,990
This sucks.

316
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,250
[AKIO] You think it's just me?

317
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:14,410
I could have a whole network
in the manor.

318
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:17,460
Everyone else here already
let Fuyuki's Blacklist

319
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,340
comb through
their personal info.

320
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:22,710
When the suspicion around you
grew too large to ignore,

321
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,590
we were all subject to doubt,

322
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:27,760
so we went through
every last person in our employ.

323
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:30,850
You're the only one
we haven't checked.

324
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,640
You did this alone.

325
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:36,310
[AKIO] Does that mean
they checked you too, Doc?

326
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:38,440
[SAKURAZAWA] Sure did.
I've got nothing to hide.

327
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:43,570
So why did you do it, Akio?

328
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:46,360
You know full well the master
gives no quarter

329
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:48,320
to those who would turn
their back on the clan.

330
00:15:48,410 --> 00:15:50,700
Once he gets home
and he has the info he needs,

331
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:51,910
you will be executed.

332
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,700
We can't bail you
out of this one.

333
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:57,580
Did you just hate working
for the Kagemoris?

334
00:15:57,660 --> 00:16:00,330
Can't say I love this life
of crime we live myself.

335
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:03,170
I'd quit in a heartbeat
if I had a way out.

336
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:04,550
But still!

337
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:07,760
If I did, you'd never see me
sell out my friends!

338
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:10,550
[sighs]

339
00:16:11,510 --> 00:16:14,760
So why'd you do it, Akio?

340
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:18,230
[Akio sighs]

341
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:22,570
[AKIO] Look, you know
what's wrong with me.

342
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,860
My body's been messed up
since birth,

343
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:26,740
so I can't feel any pain.

344
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:30,870
As a kid,
it made me unstoppable.

345
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,370
I didn't know
my physical limits,

346
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:36,790
so no one could ever beat me
in a fight.

347
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:39,500
Just as I couldn't feel
my own pain,

348
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,290
I didn't understand
the pain of others.

349
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:45,130
I'm grateful to the Kagemoris
for raising and hiring

350
00:16:45,210 --> 00:16:46,710
a delinquent like me.

351
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:49,840
If I'd gone
into the world like this,

352
00:16:49,930 --> 00:16:52,010
I'm sure I would've gotten
the death sentence

353
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:53,300
a long time ago.

354
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:56,350
But living here was easy,

355
00:16:56,430 --> 00:16:58,480
because everyone else
is crazy, too.

356
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:00,940
With all these weird daemons,

357
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,560
there's never been
a dull moment.

358
00:17:02,650 --> 00:17:03,560
[Midori grunts]

359
00:17:04,570 --> 00:17:06,440
I even had my siblings.

360
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,940
You guys were
like a family to me.

361
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:11,820
And that was fun, I guess.

362
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:16,370
But it still felt
like something was missing.

363
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,910
That "something"
never disappeared.

364
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,210
And each day,
with every step I took, it grew.

365
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:29,130
Eventually, I searched online
for people like me.

366
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,380
And wouldn't you know,
there really was a community

367
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:34,600
for us freaks
who couldn't feel pain.

368
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:37,810
On the forums,

369
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:41,060
I found someone who might be
one of my parents.

370
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,310
♪

371
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,560
I felt an emotion
I had never felt before.

372
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:50,240
Don't tell me, you reached out?

373
00:17:52,490 --> 00:17:53,660
So it was them.

374
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,530
They put these ideas
in your head.

375
00:17:56,910 --> 00:18:00,000
Akio! Your parents
abandoned you as a kid.

376
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,580
What do you get
out of seeing them now?

377
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:02,750
Why would you bother?

378
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:04,460
They might just be
trying to use you

379
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:05,630
for their own benefit!

380
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:08,050
[AKIO] Natsuki, I need a favor.

381
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:11,510
Let Mountain God go. Right now.

382
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,800
What? You know
that's not happening.

383
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,470
Fuyuki has to get their info.

384
00:18:16,010 --> 00:18:19,640
[AKIO] I beg you.
Mountain God will be destroyed.

385
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,850
They'll die.

386
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:23,560
[NATSUKI]
Destroyed? Who would do that?

387
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,980
No one here has any reason
to hurt your relics.

388
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,400
Not after
you've already dissolved

389
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,360
your contract with them.

390
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:31,230
So what are you talking about?

391
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,690
[running footsteps]

392
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:34,780
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[panting]

393
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:36,200
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[panting]

394
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:37,740
-One, two.
-[BUNBUN] Found them!

395
00:18:37,830 --> 00:18:39,290
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

396
00:18:39,370 --> 00:18:41,330
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two. One, two.
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

397
00:18:41,410 --> 00:18:43,250
Good, Mountain God
survived the fall.

398
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,120
Even if by a hare's breadth!

399
00:18:45,210 --> 00:18:46,130
[both whooping]

400
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:48,040
I'm sorry about this, friends,

401
00:18:48,130 --> 00:18:51,380
but we've gotta take a hop
to Fuyuki for interrogation.

402
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:54,130
Gotta roll up my little sleeves!

403
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,300
[grunting]

404
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,010
-[TSUGAI 1] Heave-Ho!
-[TSUGAI 2] Heave-Ho!

405
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,100
[TSUGAI 1] Huh?

406
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,470
♪

407
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:08,020
It's gonna...

408
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:12,230
-[both gasp]
-[Bunbun grunting]

409
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,990
-[explosion]
-[both gasp]

410
00:19:15,860 --> 00:19:17,370
-[JIN] Mm...
-[gasps]

411
00:19:18,370 --> 00:19:19,990
[rumbling]

412
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,090
[tsugais grunting]

413
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,050
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

414
00:19:31,130 --> 00:19:33,670
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

415
00:19:35,260 --> 00:19:36,720
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

416
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:39,180
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[both] Mm...

417
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,220
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...

418
00:19:41,970 --> 00:19:43,020
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

419
00:19:43,310 --> 00:19:44,390
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

420
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:45,480
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

421
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:46,520
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

422
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:47,560
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...

423
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:48,600
[Bunbun coughs]

424
00:19:49,310 --> 00:19:51,690
Hey, Heave-Ho?
That kinda hurts, you know.

425
00:19:51,770 --> 00:19:52,730
[TSUGAI 1] One, two...

426
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:54,900
But you two are fine,
aren't you?

427
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:56,780
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four...
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...

428
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:59,740
Oh, good. It was worth it.
[grunting]

429
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:01,530
-Ouchies.
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two...

430
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:04,200
[BUNBUN] It's busted.
I can't walk.

431
00:20:04,790 --> 00:20:06,580
[breathes shakily]

432
00:20:07,210 --> 00:20:09,670
Yamakaze is shattered.

433
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:11,290
Hm?

434
00:20:12,710 --> 00:20:15,670
Where's Tanikaze?
They're not here!

435
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,520
[squelching]

436
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,850
[squelching continues]

437
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,550
♪

438
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:00,470
[JIN] We're on our way
to the scene.

439
00:21:01,090 --> 00:21:03,430
Something blew up
near the main gate.

440
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,350
Has anything changed there?

441
00:21:05,430 --> 00:21:07,220
Nothing to report right now.

442
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:10,230
We're gonna stay on high alert
in the infirmary.

443
00:21:10,730 --> 00:21:12,520
[BABAMARU] A daemon attack?

444
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:14,020
Too early to say.

445
00:21:14,110 --> 00:21:17,150
[BABAMARU] That's the problem
with a manor like this.

446
00:21:17,230 --> 00:21:18,610
With so many daemons,

447
00:21:18,690 --> 00:21:21,360
we can't tell
when an outsider arrives.

448
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:23,450
-[door slides open]
-[NATSUKI] Mm?

449
00:21:23,530 --> 00:21:24,620
♪

450
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,370
Hold on. What's this?

451
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,370
That's Tanikaze.

452
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,210
How did they get here?

453
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,960
[running footsteps]

454
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:47,560
[tsugais yelling]

455
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,060
Everybody!

456
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:53,100
-Get down!
-[Midori grunts]

457
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:57,360
[♪ closing theme song playing]

458
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:30,410
[NATSUKI] He protected you
like he should.

459
00:23:30,490 --> 00:23:34,000
[KEN] "We're all the same.
None of us can live alone."

460
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:37,880
[ASA] Being betrayed by someone
this close really stings.
